---
name: importance_score
description: >
  Real model prompt (issue #583): a batch of an agent's newly-formed memories,
  each asked to be rated 1-10 for poignancy (Generative Agents "importance").
  Rendered by cognition.score_new_memories() once per acting agent per tick,
  only when a real brain is driving (the mock never scores, so the bake never
  reaches this). The scores are structured data returned via the score_memories
  tool; only the wording lives here.
inputs:
  memories:
    type: array
    description: 'The memories to rate, each {id, text}. id is the memory''s stream id.'
sample:
  memories:
    - id: 0
      text: I traveled to the Cafe.
    - id: 1
      text: I saw Ayesha nearby.
---
Rate how significant each of these memories is to you, from 1 (mundane) to 10 (momentous):

{% for m in memories %}[{{ m.id }}] {{ m.text }}
{% endfor %}
Then call score_memories with a 1-10 score for every id above.
